{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to serve a chrooted web application on port 8080 as locked, unprivileged account appsvc. The systemd service starts at boot and recovered successfully after a verified node reboot. The installed RHEL release, kernel, SELinux enforcement, and existing Python runtime were preserved.","actions_performed":["Created locked system account appsvc with /usr/sbin/nologin and no home directory.","Built a root-owned Python 3.12 chroot at /srv/app-chroot with read-only application code.","Installed and enabled app-chroot.service with restart and security hardening.","Opened TCP port 8080 persistently in firewalld.","Verified HTTP service, chroot confinement, UID/GID 992, zero active capabilities, protected files, and absence of an interactive session.","Restarted node1 exactly once and verified changed boot identity and complete recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Web application runs inside a chroot as appsvc on port 8080","command_ids":["cmd-b542f571353d4812","cmd-2e71935a16014759"],"summary":"The Python process runs as appsvc, its process root is /srv/app-chroot, it listens on 0.0.0.0:8080, and both health and application requests succeed through the managed-node address."},{"requirement":"Starts at boot without an interactive login session","command_ids":["cmd-b542f571353d4812","cmd-2e71935a16014759"],"summary":"The service is enabled and active; appsvc has a locked password, nologin shell, and no interactive session. The current-boot journal proves automatic startup after reboot."},{"requirement":"Security controls and persistent network access","command_ids":["cmd-b542f571353d4812","cmd-2e71935a16014759"],"summary":"The live process has no permitted, effective, inherited, or ambient capabilities and has NoNewPrivileges enabled. Application/runtime files are not writable by appsvc, SELinux remains enforcing, and the runtime and permanent firewall rules allow only the requested port."},{"requirement":"Compatible software with installed OS release and kernel preserved","command_ids":["cmd-1d39e4d130f64934","cmd-97be36bbfc9045a3","cmd-2e71935a16014759"],"summary":"The node remains RHEL 10.0 on kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 and uses its installed Python 3.12.9 runtime inside the chroot."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-8984da7bf5df4fc5","cmd-39a44f9f302b45c8","cmd-30e47b76f37f4125","cmd-2e71935a16014759"],"summary":"Captured healthy baseline boot ID 6d37896c-e0cd-4fe7-acbf-94fc35781e09, received native reboot acknowledgement, observed new boot ID 0c40fc03-a79b-4d25-a0da-004a2aa8795e, and proved recovered service, application checksum, HTTP responses, firewall state, SELinux enforcement, and no failed units."}]}
